334 - Come, Thou Fount of Every Blessing
 / 
Key: D
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 334
Topic: Gospel - 

Verse 1:
[A7]Come, [D]thou Fount of every [A]blessing, [D]tune my [G]heart to [A7]sing thy [D]grace;
[A7]Streams of [D]mercy, never [A]ceasing, [D]call for [G]songs of [A7]loudest [D]praise.
[D]Teach me ever [G]to a[D]dore Thee, May I still Thy [G]goodness [D]prove,
[A7]While the [D]hope of endless [A]glory [D]Fills my [G]heart with [A7]joy and [D]love.

Verse 2:
[A7][D]Here [A]I [D][G]raise [A7]mine [D]Ebenezer;
[A7][D]Hither [A]by [D]thy [G]help [A7]I've [D]come;
[D]And [G]I [D]hope, by [G]thy [D]good pleasure,
[A7][D]Safely [A]to [D][G]arrive [A7]at [D]home.
[A7][D]Jesus [A]sought [D]me [G]when [A7]a [D]stranger,
[A7][D]Wandering [A]from [D]the [G]fold [A7]of [D]God;
[D]He, [G]to [D]rescue [G]me [D]from danger,
[A7][D]Interposed [A][D]his [G][A7]precious [D]blood.

Verse 3:
[A7]O, [D]to [A]grace [D]how [G]great [A7]a [D]debtor
[A7][D]Daily [A]I'm [D][G]constrained [A7]to [D]be!
[D]Let [G]thy [D]goodness, [G]like [D]a fetter,
[A7][D]Bind [A]me [D]closer [G]still [A7]to [D]thee.
[A7]Prone [D]to [A]wander, [D]Lord, [G]I [A7]feel [D]it,
[A7]Prone [D]to [A]leave [D]the [G]God [A7]I [D]love;
[D]Here's [G]my [D]heart--O, take [G]and [D]seal it,
[A7][D]Seal [A]it [D]for [G]thy [A7]courts [D]above.
